>>>>> On Fri, 15 Apr 1994 13:39:35 +0000, john@pomack.demon.co.uk (John Sotiropoulos) said:
	John> Bcc:  
	John> Followup-To: 

	John> I'm trying to understand the relationship between OMG CORBA and DCE and I have
	John> recently read that "some organisations build CORBA on top of DCE". Does anyone
	John> know anything relevant?

Check out DEC/Object Broker, HP/DOMF, or IBM/DSOM for examples of DCE-based
CORBA implementations. Or for more public information, check out the CORBA
joint interoperability proposal (OMG doc 94-3-5.ps).  Although our high level
framework allows for the negotiation of common protocols other than DCE, we do
fully define a CORBA-to-DCE mapping and an NDR for achieving heterogeneous
interoperability between ORBs using DCE.

	John> In such environments, does application developent require the presence of two
	John> IDL compilers (CORBA and DCE)?

Not necessarily, you can directly generate DCE/NDR from CORBA/IDL if you
happen to be familiar with the DCE marshaling SPI.

	John> Is it possible to encapsulate code containing DCE threads and RPCs in a CORBA
	John> client or server objects as a object methods?

You can map a CORBA interface onto a DCE interface. Each CORBA operation
invocation can, thus, execute as a thread and issue an RPC call.

	John> What do people think in general about the symbiosis of DCE and CORBA?

Looks to me like a happy marriage between object technology and industry standard
client/server technology :-)

	John> -- 
	John> John Sotiropoulos

