The current version of DEC/ObjectBroker, 2.1, is not implemented on
top of DCE.  Rumor has it that it was at one point in the past, but
the DCE portion was removed for performance and maintainability
reasons.

The next version of DEC/ObjectBroker, 2.5, will not be implemented on
top of DCE.  My guess is that it will be a while before ObjectBroker
runs on top of DCE.

Interoperability between ORBs defined as a DCE layer sucks and will
probably never fly.  Of course, this is an old argument.

>Looks to me like a happy marriage between object technology and
>industry standard >client/server technology :-)

Snort!  The only thing that DCE has going for it is that Microsoft
picked it as its technology base for Distributed OLE.  Otherwise, it
would be even less of a sucess than OSF/1 (though more than OSF DME).

regards,
