In article <Ahk2fCOSMUQdN095Eu@transarc.com> Craig_Everhart@transarc.com writes:
   DCE RPC uses a ``receiver-makes-right''  representation.  Presumably the
   receiver always knows what the sender's representation is, knowing how
   to interpret the tag.  I can't comment on what happens if the protocol
   is extended to include a new representation. 

I believe this is a fundamental difference between DCE RPC and ONC
RPC.  In DCE, there is an obvious performance advantage between
compatible systems (ie, no conversion); but, every system has to know
how to perform conversion for every type of data representation.  In
ONC, there is always some cost associated with conversion to XDR; but,
that's the only "foreign" data representation the systems need to
know.
