In <1994Apr3.144347.27715@cgh.cgh.com> paul@cgh.cgh.com (Paul Homchick) writes:
>My problem is that when a client dies unexpectedly, the server thread
>also seems to die.

DCE tries very hard to preserve local function call semantics.  So yes,
if a client dies DCE will try to send the same signal over to the appropriate
thread in the server.  If you have a critical section in your server that
you need to protect from cancellations, do this:
	#include <pthread.h>

	int cancelmode;

	cancelmode = pthread_setcancel(CANCEL_OFF);
	/* ...critical section here... */
	if (cancelmode == CANCEL_ON)
	    (void)pthread_setcancel(CANCEL_ON);

	/r$


