back to OSF later this month.

Anyone else out there think that doing a threads AES at this stage may
be a masterpiece of misplaced effort?  My reasons for thinking so:

1)  The IEEE P1003.4a spec is not yet final

2)  OSF has said they're committed to supporting P1003.4a when it is
final (in both DCE and OSF/1).

I really think the last thing we need now is a spec that stands at
least some chance of not being in sync with P1003.4a, thus leaving
developers wondering what they should support, and putting OSF in the
position of immediately (potentially) violating their own spec when
they move to support the final P1003.4a.

[I know, I know, OSF is not exactly in the software development biz
any more, but the general point stands.]

Comments?

