I have recently been putting much thought into 
naming conventions within a DCE application.
Specifically, the naming of functions within  
DCE to aid in maintaining the application and
to foster re-use of the functions in other   
applications.

I have surveyed most of the books out there and
scanned source code of sample examples that were
available. About the only "standard" naming
convention I saw was that the DCE functions (RPCs)
were made up of the interface name followed by a 
descriptive name of the DCE function.

An example would be a server that defines an interface
called "db". All DCE functions within that server 
would have "db" as the prefix (i.e. db_load, db_insert,
etc).

I see as a positive with this convention in that I can
tie a specific DCE function name to an interface. But   
that is also a negative. What if after, or during, the
design phase I decide to move that function out of that
interface to a different one?

Anyone else thinking of this kind of stuff?


